From tru64-unix-managers  Sun Dec 31 14:05:34 1995
From: Greg King <king () reston ! ans ! net>
Date: Sun, 31 Dec 1995 14:05:34 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Power Management and Firmware Rev Level for RZ29B
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075325906803

Hello All,

DEC has provided me with the following information concerning
correct firmware rev levels and configuration settings for
RZ29B disks.  The sentence that concerns me most is the last
one, "Revision 0007 MUST have power management disabled (refer
to the TIMA blitz - changing page 0x0d byte 3 from 2 to 0)".  
Does anyone know what is being refered to or how this change
is made?

Thanks in advance,

Greg

>RZ29B
>
>   This device is fully supported in V3.2 or later. 
>   To use this device with V3.0/V3.0B the disktab entry must
>   be changed. Therefore, this drive can not be an 
>   installation device when installing V3.0 or V3.0B. 
>   This drive implements additional device specific 
>   parameters in it's cache mode page. The scu utility has
>   NOT yet been updated to handle these additional parameters.
>   For this reason do NOT use scu to alter the
>   cache mode page in this drive. 
>   Revision 0007 MUST have power management disabled
>  (refer to the TIMA blitz - changing page 0x0d
>   byte 3 from 2 to 0). 
>

