From: "Peter.Schauer" <Peter.Schauer@regent.e-technik.tu-muenchen.de>
To: Christophe Colle <colle@krtkg1.rug.ac.be>
Subject: Re: gdb and digital unix 3.2C

OSF 3.2C strips all debugging symbols from startup files and shared libraries,
and gdb-4.15 is unable to deal with it.
Below is a bunch of patches that handle all known gdb-4.15/OSF-3.2C problems,
they will be part of the next GDB release.

From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Dec 29 16:59:11 1995
From: mclaughl () nssdc ! gsfc ! nasa ! gov
Date: Fri, 29 Dec 1995 16:59:11 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY - Dump/Semmaphore Error
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075325906798



 Once again I received many timely and informative
 answers from the members of this list, THANKS :)

 Original Post:

> Recently I upgraded one of our 3000/600's from OSF/1 v3.0
> to DEC Unix v3.2C.  Everything went well except now the
> dump command wont work.  Here's the output:
>
> dump: Date of this level 0 dump: Thu Dec 28 10:12:43 1995 EST
> dump: Date of last level 0 dump: the start of the epoch
> dump: Dumping /dev/rrz3a (/) to /dev/nrmt0h
> dump: Mapping (Pass I) [regular files]
> dump: Mapping (Pass II) [directories]
> dump: cannot get semaphores
> get_semaphore(): semget() for fifo_free_semid: No space left on device
> dump: SIGTERM received - - Try rewriting

Thanks to:
amy amy@aloha.nascom.nasa.gov
Dr. Tom Blinn tpb@zk3.dec.com
Dale Cook cdm@hyperk.com
Knut Helleboe Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com 
Tim W. Janes janes@signal.dra.hmg.gb 
Todd Kover kovert@umiacs.UMD.EDU

The Solution:

 Add more semaphores with the semmns and semmni variables
 in the /sys/include/sys/param.h (or the /sys/conf/HOST)
 file.  Also, to determine the number of semmaphores being
 used and total number allocated use ipcs, ipcrm, and
 "sysconfig -q ipc" (very helpful man pages for each command).

 Once again, thanks a bunch.  Hope I included everyone.

Steve Mc
mclaughl@nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov

