Subject: SUMMARY: password server for DU-3.2C
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075325906681

hi managers,
> i've got poppassd with OSF1 support, compiled and ran from inetd.  
> "waitpid()" just hangs waiting for the child that execl "/bin/yppasswd".

thanks to Bill Gianopoulos <wag@swl.msd.ray.com>

"yppasswd" needs a modification in order to read from a pipe. "poppasswd" 
should call this modified "yppasswd" ("popyppass" here) on execl(...

in poppasswd.c in procedure "dochild (master, slavedev, user)" :

   /* Fork /bin/passwd. */

   if (execl(PASSWD_PATH, "passwd", user, (char*)0) < 0) {
      syslog(LOG_ERR, "can't exec %s: %m", PASSWD_PATH);
      return(0);
   }

where :

#define PASSWD_PATH     "/usr/local/etc/popyppass"

(or wherever your modified yppasswd binary is)
i'm attaching Makefile and sources to build this (easy to compile on DU).
this is uuencoded pass.tar.Z .

