There are three workarounds and two possible causes.   The
three workarounds are:

	make /tmp a real directory

	copy the /tmp file to /etc/sysconfigtab

	edit /etc/sysconfigtab manually

The two possible causes are:

	It's a bug, as it ought to work but fails under this condition.

	It's a feature, as it preempts race conditions in /tmp which 
	could be exploited.

